    "text": "HomeownerHub doesn't send collection notices or lien letters. You send them yourself or through your attorney, then record them here. To build a letter from the ledger, see draft a collections letter; printing it records it here for you.\nActions can't be edited or deleted once saved. To fix a mistake, add a note.\nYou can't mark a case \"Written off\" or pick a stage by hand after the case is open. The stage moves only when you record an action that matches it.\n\"Payment received\" and \"Payment plan agreed\" are notes on the file only. They don't record money. Record the payment on the Dues page, and set up the plan in payment plans.\nOnce a case is at \"Board authorized suit\", \"With attorney — presuit\" or \"Suit filed\", automatic dues reminders stop emailing that owner.",
