    "articleId": "violations-hearing-cured",
    "sectionId": "good-to-know",
    "heading": "Good to know",
    "text": "Florida (Fla. Stat. § 720.305(2)(e)): no fine or suspension if the violation is cured before the hearing, or cured the way the written notice asked.\nCalifornia (Civ. Code § 5855(c)): the owner may cure before the meeting. The board can’t impose discipline if the owner cured before the meeting, or, when the fix takes longer than the notice period, gave a financial commitment to cure.\nOther states: HomeownerHub has no loaded statute text on this. Check your governing documents, and ask your association’s attorney.\nGeneral information from the statute text, not legal advice.",
