    "text": "Florida: a board meeting notice must be posted in the community at least 48 hours ahead (Fla. Stat. § 720.303(2)(c)1). If you mail or deliver it instead of posting it, give 7 days. Special assessments or parcel-use rule changes need 14 days (§ 720.303(2)(c)2). Owners' meetings need 14 days (§ 720.306(5)).\nCalifornia: for an annual meeting where directors are elected, § 5115 sets the election notice and ballot deadlines. For other meeting notice periods, check your bylaws.\nTexas, Georgia and other states: the notice period isn't loaded in HomeownerHub. Check your bylaws.\nThe box is general information, not legal advice.\nThe calendar invite contains only your association's name, the meeting type, date, time and place. It holds no owner's details.\nSent it already? The button changes to Send another notice.",
