    "sectionId": "what-happens-next",
    "heading": "What happens next",
    "text": "Each step shows Done, To do, Check or Waiting. Check means something doesn't match the rule, and the step says what.\nThe checklist shows one date to watch, with a countdown.\nIn California, that's when the § 5300(a) window opens or closes. The annual budget report goes out 30 to 90 days before the fiscal year ends. For a calendar year, that's October 2 to December 1.\nIn Florida, once a meeting is linked, it's the last day to send the meeting notice: 7 days before the meeting if mailed or delivered. If special assessments will be considered, it's 14 days, and the notice must also be posted on the property.\nOtherwise, it's the day the budget year starts.\nDuring budget season, the dashboard shows a Budget season card for each budget still being adopted, with its next step and date. The season runs from 120 days before the budget year until 30 days into it.",
