    "text": "Reports count posted entries only. Draft entries don't show up until they are posted.\nThe balance sheet shows today unless you pick another date. Total equity includes net income so far this period.\nThe income statement has three ways to count: Accrual (income and expenses when billed), Cash (only entries that moved cash) and Modified accrual (income when collected, expenses when billed). Accrual is the default.\nIn budget vs. actual, a positive variance is good news: income above plan, or spending below it.\nCash flow covers operating and reserve cash, grouped by where each movement came from, from opening to closing balance.\nYou can't download these reports from their pages. For a PDF board packet with the balance sheet, income statement and cash flow, open the Periods tab. For a monthly email to the board, see the monthly board report.\nA posted entry can't be edited or deleted. On the entry's page, Reverse posts an equal and opposite entry dated today, and the original stays on the books marked reversed.\nFor the reserve balance, contributions against the budget and draws in one place, see check your reserves.\nThe Accounts tab lists your chart of accounts. You can read it, but you can't add or change accounts there.",
