    "heading": "Steps",
    "text": "Open Tickets, then select Records requests.\nEach request shows what the owner asked for, the format they prefer, the day it was received and a deadline chip. Red means the deadline has passed. Amber means it is due within 3 days. Check your bylaws means no deadline is loaded for your state or for this kind of record.\nSelect What the statute says to read the exact words of the law the deadline comes from.\nSelect Open conversation to reply to the owner. Say when and how they can see the records.\nIf the owner asked for the owner list, select Records-request roster. It makes the copy of the roster you are allowed to hand over.\nWhen the owner has the records, select Mark fulfilled. Optional: note how you provided them. Then select Confirm.",
