    "sectionId": "good-to-know",
    "heading": "Good to know",
    "text": "The notice lists the insurance company, the limit, the deductible and the end date of the master policy in force. It never shows the premium, the policy number or your notes.\nWith no master policy on record, those lines are left in brackets for you to fill in.\nIt suggests owners ask their agent about an HO-6 policy (or HO-3 for a single-family home) and loss assessment coverage.\nYour governing documents decide what the association insures and what each owner insures. The notice says so, and quotes no statute.\nGeneral information, not insurance or legal advice.",
